# System Operations Rules

## Sudo Usage Restriction
- **NEVER** use `sudo` under any circumstances
- All commands **SHALL** be done in userspace
- Avoid elevated privileges unless absolutely necessary and authorized

## Userspace Operations
- Use user-level tools and commands
- Install software in user directories when possible
- Use virtual environments for Python projects
- Use `pip install --user` for user-level package installation
- Use `npm install -g` with user-level npm configuration

## Alternative Approaches
- Use virtual environments for Python development
- Use user-level package managers when available
- Use `--user` flags for installation commands
- Configure tools to work without elevated privileges
- Use containerization (Docker) for isolated environments

## Security Best Practices
- Principle of least privilege
- Avoid running commands as root
- Use user-level configurations and directories
